"use strict";(self.webpackChunkspa_template=self.webpackChunkspa_template||[]).push([[544],{1544:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"created":"2016-04-09T13:32:00","modified":"2016-04-09T13:32:00","id":1029,"title":"Created lski-events a micro events API for the browser","article":"<p>Whilst trying to remove the reliance on jQuery from some of my work I noticed one area that was creating alot of headache was adding addEventListeners throughout my code as jQuery does alot of donkey work for you.</p>\\n<p>So I was missing some of the advanced features of &#39;on&#39; such as the filter option to exclude bubbling events depending on what fired it e.g. a button or the ability to add a single run listener that only fired once etc. So I decided to recreate something similar.</p>\\n<p>Lski-Events is a micro events library for the browser that is less than 4kb minified but offers lots of features:</p>\\n<ul>\\n<li>Single run event handlers</li>\\n<li>Multiple event attachments in single call</li>\\n<li>Delegated events via a selector</li>\\n<li>Flexible target element arguments: either an Element, Elements or a query selector</li>\\n<li>The ability to trigger events</li>\\n<li>Custom events</li>\\n<li>Normalisation of behaviour between browsers</li>\\n<li>Alias method names that mimic those in jQuery</li>\\n<li>IE8 support (requires an extra plugin that is bundled with this package)</li>\\n</ul>\\n<p>It is available on bower, <a href=\\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/lski-events\\">npm</a> and the source code is available on <a href=\\"https://github.com/lski/lski-events\\">GitHub</a>. </p>\\n","showInResults":true,"tags":["javascript","events"]}')}}]);